---
description: Clicksmith agent factory — verification, boundaries, and skip rules
alwaysApply: true
---

Clicksmith is an Electron recorder with a Python image-service and an Express API. Cloud Agents run Linux and cannot drive OS hooks or Geometry Dash.

Before claiming a change works, read `.cursor/skills/verify-clicksmith/SKILL.md` and the matching file under `.cursor/skills/verify-clicksmith/features/`. Drive the real lane. Capture evidence under `.cursor/skills/verify-clicksmith/artifacts/`. A passing compile is not proof.

Lanes:

- `ui`: verify renderer at Vite, `data-testid` handles, Playwright or computer-use
- `api`: backend `/health` + `/api/v1/profiles`, image-service `/match`
- `desktop`: real Electron + `uiohook-napi` / `robotjs` — skip on Cloud Agents
- `game`: Geode adapter `:27737` — skip on Cloud Agents

If a path is unreachable, write `SKIP desktop` or `SKIP game` with the attempted command. Do not substitute another lane.

Renderer (`client/src/renderer`) must not import Electron main. Main (`client/src/main`) must not import renderer. `nodeIntegration: true` is forbidden. Run `bash scripts/check-boundaries.sh` after process-boundary edits.

Do not ask the user to run the app, paste screenshots, or confirm routine next steps. Launch, doctor, drive, and show evidence. Reserve questions for irreversible or secret-gated actions.

pstack `/poteto-mode` is the preferred router when the plugin is loaded. If it is missing (common on Cloud Agents), follow `docs/pstack/README.md` and `.cursor/skills/clicksmith-factory/SKILL.md` instead of improvising.
